# FlintTrade — tick-engine

> High-performance tick processing engine — Rust core with Python bindings via PyO3. Read `packages/core/ticks/CLAUDE.md` first.

## Absorbs
- raptorbt → tick-level backtest patterns (reference only)

## Depends on: none (standalone Rust + PyO3 package; exposes a `tick_engine` Python module)

## Build
- `maturin develop` — develop install (links the Rust build into the active Python env)
- `maturin build --release` — produce a release wheel under `dist/`

## Rules
- Read root CLAUDE.md for project-wide rules.
- Rust code lives in `src/`; Python bindings + tests in `python/` and `tests/`.
- Never reference specific brokers — the tick engine processes anonymous OHLCV / tick streams only.
- Tests live in `packages/core/ticks/tests/`. Add Rust unit tests inline with `#[cfg(test)]` and Python integration tests as `test_*.py`.
- Cross-platform: code must compile cleanly on Windows, macOS, and Linux (CI matrix). If a feature needs a platform-specific dependency, gate it with `cfg(target_os = …)`.
- Update root CHANGELOG.md for any API surface change (added/removed exports, signature changes).
- Branch: main (pre-release, all commits to main).
